Theorem L-3: Effect lattice dimension vs EffectSummary contract record reconciliation

  Preconditions:
    - The Effect LATTICE DIMENSION is the per-variable 3-flag product
      over {may_alloc, may_share, may_throw} per Annex E §AIMS.7
      (height 3; componentwise OR join)
    - The EffectSummary CONTRACT RECORD is the per-function 7-flag derivation
      over {may_allocate, may_deallocate, may_share, may_throw,
      has_unbounded_stack, may_read_inaccessible, alloc_only_on_slow_path}
      per Annex E §AIMS IC-5 (7 fields)
    - The two are NOT the same algebra (per Annex E §AIMS.7 CRITICAL note)
    - EffectSummary is computed from INSTRUCTIONS + callee contracts
      per Annex E §AIMS IC-5 derivation procedure, NOT joined componentwise
      from per-variable EffectClass values

  Soundness property:
    Effect lattice dimension (per-variable; Annex E §AIMS.7):

      Effect_dim = <may_alloc: Bool, may_share: Bool, may_throw: Bool>

      Carrier: 3-bit flag product
      Ordering: componentwise Bool implication
      Join: componentwise OR
      Height: 3

    EffectSummary contract record (per-function; Annex E §AIMS IC-5):

      EffectSummary = <
        may_allocate: Bool,
        may_deallocate: Bool,
        may_share: Bool,
        may_throw: Bool,
        has_unbounded_stack: Bool,
        may_read_inaccessible: Bool,
        alloc_only_on_slow_path: Bool
      >

    Reconciliation claim:

      EffectSummary IS NOT joinOver(per-variable Effect_dim)

      Specifically:
        (a) The 4 EffectSummary fields beyond the shared 3-flag overlap
            (may_deallocate, has_unbounded_stack, may_read_inaccessible,
            alloc_only_on_slow_path) are NOT lattice-joined from
            per-variable state:
              - may_deallocate: derived from callee contracts +
                instruction-stream analysis (Owned params, Set/SetTag,
                analysis showing owned -> dead transitions)
              - has_unbounded_stack: derived from unbounded-recursion detection
              - may_read_inaccessible: derived from global / thread-local /
                non-arg reads
              - alloc_only_on_slow_path: derived POST-REALIZATION (after
                step 10) per Annex E §AIMS IC-5 timing clause
        (b) Per-variable Effect on call results (ALL = {alloc, share, throw})
            does NOT poison the caller's EffectSummary
            per Annex E §AIMS.7 CRITICAL note
        (c) refine() (TF-6) does NOT narrow per-variable EffectClass from
            call results; narrowing is precision work, not correctness work
        (d) The 3-flag overlap (may_alloc, may_share, may_throw) IS sourced
            from instructions + callee contracts via OR join over the
            instruction stream, NOT joined from per-variable EffectClass

      Closes gemini S01-R0-F2 arity-mismatch finding: the prior framing
      (which appeared to imply EffectSummary = per-variable-join) is
      explicitly rejected; the canonical derivation is INSTRUCTION-STREAM
      + CALLEE-CONTRACT-INHERITED per Annex E §AIMS IC-5.

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-02 + sec-06 (IC-5 derivation correctness)

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (validates the 3-flag dimension's join properties)
      monotonicity (validates EffectSummary OR-join over instruction stream
                    preserves monotonicity per L-6)

